{"html":"<p>JavaScript runs every interactive web page, and React is JavaScript. You don&#39;t need all of the language to start, but you need these basics solid: variables, a few types, functions, arrays and objects.</p>\n<h2 id=\"variables-let-and-const\">Variables: let and const</h2>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">let</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> count </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 0</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">; </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// can be reassigned</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">count </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> count </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">+</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 1</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">const</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> name</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\"> \"Ana\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">; </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// can't be reassigned</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>Use <code>const</code> by default, and <code>let</code> only when the value really changes. Avoid the old <code>var</code>: it ignores block scope and causes confusing bugs.</p>\n<p><code>const</code> stops <strong>reassigning</strong> the variable, not changing what&#39;s inside it. A <code>const</code> array can still get new items with <code>push</code>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"types\">Types</h2>\n<div data-table-scroll><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Type</th>\n<th>Example</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>number</code></td>\n<td><code>42</code>, <code>3.5</code> (one type for both)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>string</code></td>\n<td><code>&quot;hi&quot;</code>, <code>&#39;hi&#39;</code>, <code>`hi`</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>boolean</code></td>\n<td><code>true</code>, <code>false</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>undefined</code></td>\n<td>A variable with no value yet</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>null</code></td>\n<td>&quot;Nothing&quot;, set on purpose</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>object</code></td>\n<td><code>{ name: &quot;Ana&quot; }</code>, arrays</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p><code>typeof</code> tells you the type, with two famous quirks: <code>typeof null</code> is <code>&quot;object&quot;</code>, and so is <code>typeof []</code>. Use <code>Array.isArray</code> for arrays.</p>\n<h3 id=\"the-equality-trap\">The Equality Trap</h3>\n<p><code>==</code> converts types before comparing; <code>===</code> doesn&#39;t:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">1</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> ==</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\"> \"1\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">; </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// true</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">1</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> ===</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\"> \"1\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">; </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// false</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>Always use <code>===</code> and <code>!==</code>. Conversion also bites with <code>+</code>, which glues strings:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"5\"</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> +</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 3</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">; </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// \"53\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"5\"</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> -</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 3</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">; </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// 2</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><h3 id=\"truthy-and-falsy\">Truthy and Falsy</h3>\n<p>In an <code>if</code>, these values count as false: <code>false</code>, <code>0</code>, <code>&quot;&quot;</code>, <code>null</code>, <code>undefined</code> and <code>NaN</code>. <strong>Everything else is true</strong>, including <code>&quot;0&quot;</code>, <code>[]</code> and <code>{}</code>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"template-literals\">Template Literals</h2>\n<p>Backticks let you put values inside strings with <code>${…}</code>:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">const</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> message</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\"> `Hello, ${</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">name</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">}! You have ${</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">count</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">} message.`</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">;</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><h2 id=\"functions\">Functions</h2>\n<p>Two common ways to write one:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">function</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> add</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">a</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">, </span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">b</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">  return</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> a </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">+</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> b;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">}</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">const</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> multiply</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> (</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">a</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">, </span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">b</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">) </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=></span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> a </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">*</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> b; </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// arrow function</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>An arrow function with a single expression returns it without <code>return</code>. Parameters can have default values:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">function</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> greet</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">person</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\"> \"friend\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">  return</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\"> \"Hi \"</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> +</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> person;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">}</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">greet</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(); </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// \"Hi friend\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">greet</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"Ben\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">); </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// \"Hi Ben\"</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>Functions are values: you can store them in variables and pass them to other functions. That&#39;s what the array methods below rely on.</p>\n<h2 id=\"arrays\">Arrays</h2>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">const</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> prices</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> [</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">12</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">, </span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">5</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">, </span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">30</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">, </span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">8</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">];</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">prices.</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">length</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">; </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// 4</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">prices[</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">0</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">]; </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// 12</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">prices.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">at</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">-</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">1</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">); </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// 8, the last one</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">prices.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">push</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">20</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">); </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// add at the end</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>The methods you&#39;ll use constantly, especially in React:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">prices.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">map</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">((</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">p</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">) </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=></span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> p </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">*</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 2</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">); </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// [24, 10, 60, 16, 40]</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">prices.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">filter</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">((</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">p</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">) </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=></span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> p </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">></span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 10</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">); </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// [12, 30, 20]</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">prices.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">reduce</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">((</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">sum</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">, </span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">p</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">) </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=></span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> sum </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">+</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> p, </span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">0</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">); </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// 75</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">prices.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">find</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">((</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">p</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">) </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=></span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> p </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">></span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 10</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">); </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// 12</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">prices.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">includes</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">5</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">); </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// true</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">prices.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">some</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">((</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">p</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">) </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=></span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> p </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">></span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 25</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">); </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// true</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p><code>map</code> and <code>filter</code> return a <strong>new</strong> array and leave the original alone.</p>\n<p>One trap: <code>sort()</code> without a function sorts as <strong>text</strong>, so <code>[12, 20, 30, 5, 8]</code>. Pass a compare function for numbers, and copy first, because <code>sort</code> changes the array in place:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">[</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">...</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">prices].</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">sort</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">((</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">a</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">, </span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">b</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">) </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=></span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> a </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">-</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> b); </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// [5, 8, 12, 20, 30]</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><h2 id=\"objects\">Objects</h2>\n<p>An object groups named values:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">const</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> user</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> { name: </span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"Ana\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">, age: </span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">30</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">, address: { city: </span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"Lyon\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> } };</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">user.name; </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// \"Ana\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">user[</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"age\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">]; </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// 30</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">user.address.city; </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// \"Lyon\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">user.email </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\"> \"ana@example.com\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">; </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// add a property</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">Object.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">keys</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(user); </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// [\"name\", \"age\", \"address\", \"email\"]</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>Reading a missing property gives <code>undefined</code>, and reading a property <strong>of</strong> <code>undefined</code> throws. Optional chaining <code>?.</code> stops safely, and <code>??</code> gives a fallback for <code>null</code> or <code>undefined</code>:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">user.phone?.number; </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// undefined, no error</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">user.nickname </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">??</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\"> \"none\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">; </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// \"none\"</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><h2 id=\"loops\">Loops</h2>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">for</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> (</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">const</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> price</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> of</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> prices) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">  console.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">log</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(price);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">}</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">for</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> (</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">const</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> [</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">key</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">, </span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">value</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">] </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">of</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> Object.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">entries</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">({ a: </span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">1</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">, b: </span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">2</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> })) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">  console.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">log</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(key, value);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">}</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>In practice, <code>map</code>, <code>filter</code> and <code>reduce</code> replace many loops.</p>\n<h2 id=\"objects-and-arrays-are-references\">Objects and Arrays Are References</h2>\n<p>A variable holds a <strong>reference</strong> to an object, so copying the variable shares the object:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">const</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> copy</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> user;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">copy.age </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 31</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">user.age; </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// 31, it's the same object</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>This matters a lot in React, which notices changes by comparing references. You&#39;ll create new objects and arrays instead of changing them, as the next article shows.</p>\n<h2 id=\"the-answer-in-short\">The Answer in Short</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Use <code>const</code> by default, <code>let</code> when the value changes, never <code>var</code>.</li>\n<li>Compare with <code>===</code>; remember <code>&quot;5&quot; + 3</code> is <code>&quot;53&quot;</code> and which values are falsy.</li>\n<li>Write functions as declarations or arrows; functions are values you can pass around.</li>\n<li>Use <code>map</code>, <code>filter</code>, <code>reduce</code> and <code>find</code> on arrays, and sort numbers with a compare function.</li>\n<li>Read nested data safely with <code>?.</code> and <code>??</code>, and remember objects and arrays are shared by reference.</li>\n</ol>\n"}